From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:26:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] feat: voice narrows the purchase limits (set_limits,
 show_limits)

brain.md S2 / B3, the agent half: "Find hangers, under $40, arriving by Friday."

- Every command is scanned for limits first (digits only): "under / below / less than / no more
  than / up to / at most / max / budget of $N" or "N dollars/bucks" -> max_total_usd (a cap on the
  order total, so "$5 each/apiece/per ..." and "under 40 mm" are left alone), and
  "arriving / delivered / here by|before <weekday|tomorrow|today|YYYY-MM-DD>" -> deliver_by.
  They go through mandate.set_limits(source="voice") and queue show_limits; whatever is left of
  the command is routed as usual, so the example sets the limits and then searches
  ("Limits set: under $40, by Fri Oct 2. Searching the supply shops.").
- LLM tool set_limits (S2 schema: max_total_usd, deliver_by, seller_policy, all nullable); it may
  ride along with find_part in the same turn and ends the turn with its spoken line.
- Voice can't loosen: "up to $100" after $40 answers "You'd need to raise that on the panel.
  Still under $40, by Fri Oct 2." and show_limits carries the refusal.
- show_limits {intent_id, max_total_usd, deliver_by, seller_policy, refused} for the wrist chip.
- "buy it" still only opens the panel (start_checkout, unchanged).

Rebased onto integration/grok-all (c706f13): the limits pre-pass runs in `_handle_command` before
`_fast_route` and routes the rest through `_handle_command` (the rider wrapper already ran). It is
skipped for a rules or quote command, where money is about a rebate or the quote ("any rebates
up to $500?", "check this quote, is it under $2000?"). `set_limits` joins `_OWN_LINE_TOOLS` (the
early-exit tuple) and still rides along with `find_part`. `Session.id` was already upstream.
Tests: +3 (the rules/quote guard, limits then "do the whole job"). Row 0 of the priority table.

